[37m▸ Thought for 16s, 2.2k tokens[m

  Cold waves crashed on the dark rocks. Wind battered the northern shore. Thomas lived high above the spray. His lighthouse
  stood tall and white.

  Inside, a small fire crackled. Ash, his grey cat, curled on a rug. The cat yawned softly. He blinked his green eyes.

  The night grew cold and deep. A gale rattled the thick glass. Thomas climbed the spiral stairs. His heavy boots thudded on
  cold iron. Ash followed close behind him.

  The great brass lamp turned. Its bright beam cut the fog. Down below, black water churned. No ships were in sight.

  The watch was long and quiet. Thomas drank hot black tea. Ash rested on his knee.

  The fierce wind slowly died. The sky turned pale gray. Gulls called over the rocks. Thomas extinguished the lamp. He stroked
  the cat's warm back. Golden rays broke the mist.

  It was the first light of morning.

